# Build profile: minimal.
# GKI baseline + SukiSU integration only. SUSFS is compiled in
# unconditionally with CONFIG_KSU in SukiSU-Nova v3.0.0 (no compile-time
# switch); minimal-ness comes from no KPM, no candidate tunables and no
# runtime SUSFS list. See docs/phase1/BUILD_PROFILES.md.

# DIAGNOSTIC BUILD (Phase 3.2 root-cause bisect, temporary): the two previous
# L4 attempts hung at the first boot screen and left zero pstore content (a
# hang, not a panic - ramoops only records panics). Module ABI, flashing and
# packaging were systematically excluded:
#   - kernel bytes on boot_b were byte-identical to the CI Image;
#   - fixed-point module dependency analysis: only oplus_bsp_sched_ext.ko and
#     oplus_bsp_game_opt.ko (both non-boot-critical, unpublished HMBIRD
#     symbols) fail to load, with no cascade;
#   - the reference kernel (different KSU family, same flash flow) boots.
# Remaining prime suspect: the SukiSU-Nova v3.0.0 built-in integration
# (patch 0100), whose selinux-hide and task hooks run during early init.
# This build switches CONFIG_KSU off so the kernel boots without any KSU
# hooks linked in:
#   - boots  -> SukiSU-Nova integration is the root cause (choose another
#     KSU route/version next);
#   - hangs  -> the problem is in the OnePlusOSS tree or patches 0200-0300.
# Root availability is not expected in this build (no KSU); it exists only to
# isolate the boot failure. Revert this commit once the bisect concludes.
# CONFIG_KSU is not set

# Diagnostic variable (Phase 3.2): stock has HMBIRD_SCHED=y and no
# SCHED_CLASS_EXT, while gki_defconfig enables SCHED_CLASS_EXT=y. Turn SCX
# off to test whether the ext scheduler is the remaining early-boot suspect.
# CONFIG_SCHED_CLASS_EXT is not set
